     "content": "1. **Pick one principle only** for the next seven days — start with name recall, since it is the easiest to score as right or wrong.\n\n2. **Use the three-step drill** at every introduction: repeat the name immediately, retrieve it twice more within five minutes, and ask one question that creates a hook.\n\n3. **Log every attempt** in a notes app the same night: name, hook question, whether you still had the name an hour later.\n\n4. **Check your smile on video** once this week during a real call — pause the recording and look for the eye-crinkle that marks a genuine smile.\n\n5. **Review on Friday**: count your name-recall success rate. Move to the next principle — genuine interest — only once you are consistently retaining most names.",
